  "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nWe have been given the sum ${S}_{N}=139.4,$ and the first term ${a}_{1}=4.2.$ Our goal is to find $N,$ the number of terms.\n\nThe common difference $d$ can be found, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =4.7-4.2 \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 139.4 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2(4.2)+(N-1)(0.5)) \\\\ 278.8 & =N(8.4+0.5N-0.5) \\\\ 278.8 & =N(7.9+0.5N) \\\\ 278.8 & =7.9N+0.5{N}^{2} \\\\ 0.5{N}^{2}+7.9N-278.8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the equation above, the quadratic formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N & =\\frac{-7.9\\pm \\sqrt{(-7.9)^{2}-4\\cdot 0.5\\cdot (-278.8)}}{2\\cdot 0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7.9\\pm 24.9}{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $N=17$ or $N=-32.8.$ We disregard the negative solution since $N$ must be positive and integer.\n\nTherefore, our series has $N=17$ terms.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
